{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact OPS-1 head 7bf8153e671e2802dfe2d1e28948f071a2b78102 on builder/deploy-ops1-20261110, all nine artifacts, for request b380ea8c under promise f31ea829 and review request 65c6cce8. The head does what b380ea8c asks, under rulings 5b38cde5 and 28696bae. One command deploys the four tracked configurations, and one read-only smoke command checks each Worker.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `scripts/deploy.mjs`:\n  - It refuses a dirty checkout, and it checks again before each dry run and each upload. It also refuses when HEAD moves or a configuration's bytes change after the dry run.\n  - Each name needs exactly one baseline: a full deployed commit, or a previous receipt. A receipt must match its config path, Worker name and the SHA-256 of the configuration at its commit.\n  - `checkMigrations` refuses a changed or removed historical row. It refuses each new tag that `--accept-migration` does not name, and an acceptance that no configuration uses.\n  - Every dry run finishes before the first upload. Wrangler 4.147.0 runs through `npx` from a `mkdtemp` directory outside the checkout and its Git common directory, with `--keep-vars`, metrics off and `WRANGLER_CI_OVERRIDE_NAME` removed.\n  - The receipt directory must lie outside both roots, and a symlink cannot move it inside.\n  - A failure after an upload starts exits 3 with a partial record, and the batch stops with no retry or rollback, as ruling 5b38cde5 item 3 requires.\n- `bundleManifest` hashes the sorted list of names, byte counts and SHA-256 values of the dry-run output. It skips the root README.md and `.map` files, bounds the walk, and refuses symlinks and special files. The receipt says that the hash proves the dry-run output, not the upload or the kept variables.\n- `scripts/deploy-smoke.mjs`:\n  - It sends only GET and one POST to `/mcp`, with a browser User-Agent and no credentials. Redirects fail, each reply has a 10-second deadline, and a JSON body is limited to 16 KiB.\n  - Health must answer 200 three times, and only a first 503 gets a retry.\n  - `smokePolicy` takes the MCP answer and the offer from the tracked configuration only. MCP must answer 404 unless `MCP_ENABLED` is `\"true\"` and both MCP bindings exist, and then 401. A declared offer must answer 200 with the exact register, origin and definition. An omitted offer must answer 404. No argument changes either expectation.\n  - The offer reply's `v: 2` matches `CreationOffer` in `packages/client/src/creation-offer.ts`. Version 3 belongs only to the configuration value.\n- The runbook section stands before \"Roll back\". Its commands exist at the head, including `dap verify --all` (`packages/cli/src/command-verify.ts:102`). It states the secrets, the `--keep-vars` rule from ruling 5b38cde5, the migration rule, the meaning of exit 3 and the rollback limit. `.wrangler/` is in `.gitignore`, so Wrangler's temporary files under `apps/room/.wrangler/tmp` leave the checkout clean.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main df41e599 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the nine paths that the nine artifacts cover, and the primary artifact is neither stale nor retired. The last commit changes only the note and the evidence manifest.\n- Cheap checks. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes: 6 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Tests, on my own extracted copy, with no shared validation slot. `node --test scripts/deploy.test.mjs scripts/deploy-smoke.test.mjs` passes 19 of 19: 11 deployment cases and 8 smoke cases. The four named failing cases of b380ea8c are among them: a dirty checkout, a new migration tag without acceptance, health that stays 503, and an open `/mcp` on a closed configuration.\n- Evidence. The 58 files that the manifest lists match their SHA-256 values in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-11-ops1-f357-final-review`, and `SHA256SUMS` verifies. The note's gate result agrees with END 910164dc: 5,906 identities, 5,903 passes and three planned skips, all named. The two controls agree with END 36c4e2d1: each mutant fails at its named assertion.\n- CI. GitHub reports Page run 43141194766 and Card run 43141194772 as push events, attempt 1, completed and successful, at the head.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The command and the smoke check share one configuration reader and add nothing to the runtime. The tracked configuration stays the only source of variables and expectations, and the command takes no mode or variable input. Deployment from CI stays out of scope.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The command changes no secret. It writes nothing into the checkout, and its receipt and partial records hold no credential. The tests show that no input can add a Wrangler flag. Smoke is read-only and sends no credential. A partial upload is never retried or rolled back automatically.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note for a later head: the partial record goes to the scratch directory under the system temporary directory, even when `--receipt-dir` is given. The runbook says to reconcile from that record before another run, and the system can clean that directory. The command could also write the partial record to the receipt directory when that directory exists.\n\nThis approval authorizes no deployment. The planner lands the head and runs the first deployment, as b380ea8c says.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5fd24477daa8991d358ef5c9247752b0999b4de7","binding":"assigned","head":"7bf8153e671e2802dfe2d1e28948f071a2b78102","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:602433e60f3160e3833f008da42f78e231dcfe47\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f31ea829582ee76f0540c665e2c404c7456d4049\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:821c201